{"title":"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Alternate_Finish)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Alternate Finish)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Lemma\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Lemma</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nFind the least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9c990a7b70753fe475b450cb0915460af6cf64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1{\\sin 45^\\circ\\sin 46^\\circ}+\\frac 1{\\sin 47^\\circ\\sin 48^\\circ}+\\cdots+\\frac 1{\\sin 133^\\circ\\sin 134^\\circ}=\\frac 1{\\sin n^\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"509\" height=\"37\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We apply the identity \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d75faa212e8d2e246616eed6303f8e50fb5e42df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{1}{\\sin n \\sin (n+1)} &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\sin 1} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin (n+1) \\cos n - \\sin n \\cos (n+1)}{\\sin n \\sin (n+1)} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\sin 1} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\cos n}{\\sin n} - \\frac{\\cos (n+1)}{\\sin (n+1)}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\sin 1} \\cdot \\left(\\cot n - \\cot (n+1)\\right). \\end{align*}\" width=\"460\" height=\"136\" />\n</p><p>The motivation for this identity arises from the need to decompose those fractions, possibly into <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Telescoping\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Telescoping\">telescoping</a>. \n</p><p>Thus our summation becomes \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79dfa6a1b147c857e927c3fc52695c5420f19c02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=23}^{67} \\frac{1}{\\sin (2k-1) \\sin 2k} = \\frac{1}{\\sin 1} \\left(\\cot 45 - \\cot 46 + \\cot 47 - \\cdots + \\cot 133 - \\cot 134 \\right).\\]\" width=\"636\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada321f7f657517460f95349f91b1fc330c4b83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot (180 - x) = - \\cot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />, the summation simply reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d4be9b7ef6609523e02f11f5fd318b0facbde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sin 1} \\cdot \\left( \\cot 45 - \\cot 90 \\right) = \\frac{1 - 0}{\\sin 1} = \\frac{1}{\\sin 1^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"316\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095810b11bb33e311d581b5d4959399c7490300f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can make an approximation by observing the following points:\n</p><p>The average term is around the 60's which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>There are 45 terms, so the approximate sum is 60.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2bae343195081c1eca85ab6e71ade6fd9d181ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(n^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> equals approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Recall that the approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> in radians is x if x is close to zero. In this case x is close to zero. Converting to radians we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b050b39ada1b2f2d885b691ea508e251e183618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> in degrees is about sin<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e3b8f932833a1cc5a7f17ac1ff7c026492100c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{57}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> in radians, or is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e3b8f932833a1cc5a7f17ac1ff7c026492100c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{57}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> because of the approximation. What we want is apparently close to that so we make the guess that n is equal to 1 degree. Basically, it boils down to the approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/53142d0fd55c06d130761597b29a6f61912ae1b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(1)=\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" /> in degrees, convert to radians and use the small angle approximation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38367cae2a5ce30ddb33f8beabc4801a4c434ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~edited for clarity by fermat_sLastAMC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Alternate_Finish.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Alternate_Finish)\">Solution 3 (Alternate Finish)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Alternate Finish)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let S be the sum of the sequence. We begin the same as in Solution 1 to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad228c8be841e5677676ff2c6aea3ac37d6f6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\sin(1)=\\cot(45)-\\cot(46)+\\cot(47)-\\cot(48)+...+\\cot(133)-\\cot(134)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"593\" height=\"20\" />. Observe that this \"almost telescopes,\" if only we had some extra terms. Consider adding the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c3aec0cd88f2beff91a06dc20b2bf6859aac7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sin(46)\\sin(47)}+\\frac{1}{\\sin(48)\\sin(49)}+...+\\frac{1}{\\sin(134)\\sin(135)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"451\" height=\"43\" />. By the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622207507378935175ab918b1bbfdc6f16c88c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)=\\sin(180-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />, this sequence is equal to the original one, simply written backwards. By the same logic as before, we may rewrite this sequence as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c615c1e1b1f02f07cf089ca4155098f94afd5b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\sin(1)=\\cot(46)-\\cot(47)+\\cot(48)-\\cot(49)+...+\\cot(134)-\\cot(135)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"593\" height=\"20\" />,\nand when we add the two sequences, they telescope to give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d83b7a7ae301bbd6c19dce832b84f79ce3af86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2S\\sin(1)=\\cot(45)-\\cot(135)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"20\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aeb890530a2171ba1a3de468fd7017962d0a2a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{1}{\\sin(1^\\circ)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"95\" height=\"43\" />, and our angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095810b11bb33e311d581b5d4959399c7490300f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~keeper1098\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb566b37b531dbfb7a5829182933a09c9949c881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin n^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> on both sides.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717c11e4b37a217229033207fbcf71367e6faf8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     \\frac{\\sin n^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ}     &amp;= \\frac{\\sin (k+n-k)^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\\\     &amp;= \\frac{\\sin (k+n)^\\circ \\cos k^\\circ - \\sin k^\\circ \\cos (k+n)^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\end{align*}\" width=\"465\" height=\"92\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd626208998b7d813acae62e22d7f0b233f06a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = m$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is could be any number.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f39e7fb19b315bfbb826852db7817e218bbd244e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     &amp;\\quad \\ \\frac{\\sin (k+n)^\\circ \\cos k^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sin k^\\circ \\cos (k+n)^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\\\[0.5em]     &amp;=\\frac{\\sin (m+n)^\\circ \\cos m^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sin m^\\circ \\cos (m+n)^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\end{align*}\" width=\"341\" height=\"101\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lemma\">Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<pre>   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</pre>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc057f9dfd8289ad6ef910f1f3caf13d467948be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     &amp;=\\frac{\\sin (m+1)^\\circ \\cos m^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sin m^\\circ \\cos (m+1)^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ \\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\\\[0.5em]     &amp;=\\frac{\\cos m^\\circ}{\\sin m^\\circ} - \\frac{\\cos (m+1)^\\circ}{\\sin (m+1)^\\circ} \\\\[0.5em]     &amp;= \\cot m^\\circ - \\cot (m+1)^\\circ \\end{align*}\" width=\"337\" height=\"134\" />\nThe sum of all numbers could be written. Moreover, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8797411a83dc0b6f248edcce011b445bef8dc0b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot\\alpha + \\cot\\beta = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de19b17ae008abc8b34d0677d95fa8be7bb0f772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0389c1172b9511086039f5fc6d1f32ef6b9af56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     &amp;\\quad \\ \\cot 45^\\circ - \\cot 46^\\circ + \\cot 47^\\circ - \\cot 48^\\circ + \\cdots - \\cot 132^\\circ + \\cot 133^\\circ - \\cot 134^\\circ \\\\     &amp;= (\\cot 45^\\circ + \\cot 47^\\circ + \\cdots + \\cot 89^\\circ + \\cot 91^\\circ + \\dots + \\cot 133^\\circ) \\\\     &amp;\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad - (\\cot 46^\\circ + \\dots + \\cot 88^\\circ + \\cot 90^\\circ + \\cot 92^\\circ + \\dots + \\cot 134^\\circ) \\\\     &amp;= \\cot 45^\\circ - \\cot 90^\\circ \\\\     &amp;= 1 \\end{align*}\" width=\"678\" height=\"112\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dec7050aa92389359debfb8b7fda5e4146d824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, the lemma is true.\n</p><p>Q.E.D.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> could be 1. Moreover, there are no smaller positive integer less than 1 to test. Thus, the least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the given condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095810b11bb33e311d581b5d4959399c7490300f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~MaPhyCom\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II\" title=\"2000 AIME II\">2000 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016212443\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 277/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1776/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 135/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8974/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.735      1 -total\n 58.40%    7.437      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.78%    5.066      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3144:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016212443 and revision id 263401. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}